    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44343" root="&#xA;                        هم&#xA;                    " body-key="h1">
                        
                            8
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِهْتَمَّ بِالأَمْرِ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>He was grieved,</i> and <i>disquieted,
by the affair,</i> or <i>case:</i> (TA:) you say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِهْتَمَّ لَهُ</span>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِأَمْرِهِ</span>
                        <i>he was grieved for him by his affair,</i> or
<i>case.</i> (S.) [<i>He was,</i> or <i>became, anxious, disquieted,</i> or <i>grieved,</i> by it.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>He minded,</i> or
<i>attended to, the affair:</i> (MA:) <i>undertook,</i> or
<i>superintended,</i> or <i>managed, the affair.</i> (Msb.)
See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُنِىَ</span>, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عنى</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِهْتَمَّ لَهُ</span>
                        <i>He cared for,
minded,</i> or <i>regarded, him,</i> or <i>it.</i> (Har, p. 94.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِهْتَمَّ بَلَدَ كَذَا</span>
                        <i>i. q.</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِعْتَسَّهُ</span>. (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عس</span>.)

